Default an empty D7 node language to en.

The content migration group's shared_configuration maps langcode with
static_map + bypass: true, which passes any unmapped value through unchanged.
D7 sites can carry nodes whose {node}.language is the empty string rather than
und or en (70 of them on agsci), and those migrate to a node with
langcode = ''. Drupal loads field values by matching the entity's langcode
against the field tables, which the migration writes as en, so every field on
such a node resolves empty: the body, image references and everything else
render as if the node had no content at all, with no error anywhere.

Chain a non-strict default_value after the map. It treats '' as falsy and
substitutes en, while und (already mapped) and real language codes pass
through untouched.

--- a/modules/paragraphs_to_layout_builder/config/install/migrate_plus.migration_group.content.yml
+++ b/modules/paragraphs_to_layout_builder/config/install/migrate_plus.migration_group.content.yml
@@ -16,11 +16,19 @@
     vid: vid
     type: type
     langcode:
-      plugin: static_map
-      bypass: true
-      source: language
-      map:
-        und: en
+      # A handful of D7 nodes carry language = '' rather than und or en.
+      # static_map with bypass passes those through unchanged, leaving the node
+      # with an empty langcode that matches none of its field rows (written as
+      # en), so every field on it silently loads empty. default_value is not
+      # strict, so it treats '' as falsy and substitutes en while leaving real
+      # language codes untouched.
+      - plugin: static_map
+        bypass: true
+        source: language
+        map:
+          und: en
+      - plugin: default_value
+        default_value: en
     title: title
     uid: node_uid
     status: status
